 "description": "Mt. Gox stood for \"Magic: The Gathering Online eXchange\" - Jed McCaleb built it for trading game cards.\nIn 2010 he turned it into a Bitcoin exchange, and in March 2011 he sold it to Mark Karpelès.\nBy 2013 it handled over 70% of all Bitcoin transactions. In February 2014 trading stopped - about 850,000 Bitcoin were missing, worth around $450 million at the time. Karpelès was arrested in 2015.\n\nWould you have trusted it? 👇\n\nNot financial advice. Entertainment and education only.",
